<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chibinda Ilunga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chibinda Ilunga is a legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba</a> prince and hunter traditionally credited with marrying into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> royal line, in the person of the female ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lueji">Lueji</a>. He is said to have introduced the Luba model of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship">sacred kingship</a> and administration. His story is the founding tradition of the Lunda Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chibinda-ilunga.jpg" alt="Chibinda Ilunga" width="279" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edited by J.F. Ade Ajayi (ed.). · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:THE_CONGO_BASIN_AND_ANGOLA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
